From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:02:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Enable PCIe port 0 again

This reverts commit 8b979af91a56 ("arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Disable
PCIe port 0 for now").

PCIe port 0 (the BCM4388 Wi-Fi/Bluetooth module) and its DART were
disabled because the J604 device tree that enabled them stopped the
machine early in boot, before the console. Booting variants of the
device tree narrowed this down to the DART (MEASURED 2026-11-04): with
the port and m1n1's radio power-up enabled but the DART disabled, the
machine boots; enabling the DART as well brings the hang back.

The cause is the DART's register window, which was too small for the
exception records the driver accesses while resetting the DART at
probe; the previous change sizes it like the other T8132 DARTs. Enable
the port and its DART again on top of that.

TO-VERIFY: a J604 boot with this device tree (variant W1).

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 10 +++-------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index ccb3210c3b..008c746010 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -202,25 +202,21 @@
  * "guam"). m1n1 powers it through the same SMC action as pwren-gpios and
  * fills in the addresses, antenna SKU and calibration below. Port 1 is not
  * wired; port 2 (the SD card reader) stays off.
- *
- * Disabled for now: a J604 device tree that enables this port together with
- * the USB-C ports and the AOP hangs early boot, before the console. Enable
- * it again once a J604 boot with it enabled has been shown to work.
  */
 
 &pcie0_dart {
-	status = "disabled"; /* DTV-PCIE-3..5 */
+	status = "okay"; /* DTV-PCIE-3..5 */
 };
 
 &pcie0 {
 	iommu-map = <0x100 &pcie0_dart 1 1>;
-	status = "disabled"; /* DTV-PCIE-1, DTV-PCIE-2 */
+	status = "okay"; /* DTV-PCIE-1, DTV-PCIE-2 */
 };
 
 &pcie0_port0 {
 	pwren-gpios = <&smc_gpio 0x13 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>; /* DTV-PCIE-11 */
 	bus-range = <1 1>;
-	status = "disabled"; /* DTV-PCIE-6, DTV-PCIE-7 */
+	status = "okay"; /* DTV-PCIE-6, DTV-PCIE-7 */
 
 	wifi0: wifi@0,0 {
 		compatible = "pci14e4,4434"; /* DTV-WLAN-1 */
